    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0469v2</id>
    <title>Non-degeneracy of Pollard Rho Collisions</title>
    <updated>2008-08-31T16:24:38Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0469v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0808.0469v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  The Pollard Rho algorithm is a widely used algorithm for solving discrete logarithms on general cyclic groups, including elliptic curves. Recently the first nontrivial runtime estimates were provided for it, culminating in a sharp O(sqrt(n)) bound for the collision time on a cyclic group of order n. In this paper we show that for n satisfying a mild arithmetic condition, the collisions guaranteed by these results are nondegenerate with high probability: that is, the Pollard Rho algorithm successfully finds the discrete logarithm.</summary>
